
# commit-template v1 -- see .husky/prepare-commit-msg
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Conventional Commits, enforced by commitlint in the commit-msg hook.
#
#   <type>(<optional scope>): <subject>
#
#   <optional body: what changed and why>
#
#   <optional footer: BREAKING CHANGE: ..., Refs: ...>
#
# Allowed types:
#   feat      a new feature
#   fix       a bug fix
#   chore     build process, tooling, or dependency updates
#   docs      documentation changes only
#   style     formatting, whitespace (no logic change)
#   refactor  code restructuring without behavior change
#   test      adding or updating tests
#   ci        CI/CD configuration changes
#   build     build system changes
#   revert    revert a previous commit
#
# Subject rules:
#   - 100 characters maximum
#   - imperative mood ("add feature", not "added feature")
#   - no trailing period
#
# Leave a blank line between the subject and the body.
# This guidance block is discarded automatically and never reaches the commit.
# See CONTRIBUTING.md for the full guide.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
